    "turn_text": "Hello and welcome to another edition of Career Education Report. I'm Jason Altmeyer and this will be a special edition of our podcast because this was a live interview with former vice president of the United States, Mike Pence. The interview occurred in Indianapolis during the Career Education Convention on June 13th. And we were able to sit down with Vice President Pence and have a wide-ranging discussion on issues related to higher education and politics and his views on current events. And I think everyone will be interested. So keep in mind, this was before a live audience. It was a podcast recording, and we are proud to bring it to you right now. Mr. Vice President, thank you for being with us. Delighted, thank you. Why don't you, I think a good way to start would be to talk about what you've been doing for the past three and a half years. You're doing some amazing work around the world. You've started a foundation. Why don't we start there?",
