    "turn_text": "it marks introduction and people might be surprised that you were a radio talk show host before you were first elected to Congress in 2000. And I think what's most interesting about it, you, of course, are a staunch conservative unabashed in your views, but not confrontational. The time when you were in talk radio was a time of great confrontation, a time when people were very bombastic and you took a different approach to that. So what did you learn from your experience in talk radio and why did you feel like that was the right approach? And I guess do you feel like that helped or hurt your ratings as a talk show host?",
